 "description": "Price in the watchlist (Android DisplayFormat.formatDouble behind PriceFormat.price, iOS PriceFormat.formatDouble): below 10 at most four significant digits without trailing zeros (pattern «@###», tiny prices stay readable: 0.00000712), from 10 on always two decimals with the grouping of the region («83’142.00» in Switzerland). Rounding HALF_EVEN; no case sits exactly on a rounding tie (JVM and ICU decide ties of binary doubles differently). Swiss grouping: Java/CLDR gives U+2019, Foundation may give the ASCII apostrophe – compared without that one character difference (like watch_price.json). Android: the pattern «@###» exists only in the DecimalFormat of Android (ICU), not on the JVM of the unit tests – PriceFormatParityTest (JVM) checks the cases from 10 on, PriceFormatIcuTest (device) the cases below 10; iOS PriceFormatParityTests checks all.",
